# Tests

Two kinds, and the difference is absolute.

**Co-located unit tests** — `src/core/rng.test.ts`. Yours. Write as many as
you like. They are typechecked by `npm run law` because they live under
`src/`, which is what makes type-level assertions there real rather than
decorative.

**Acceptance tests** — `tests/acceptance/*.test.ts`. **Not yours.** They are
the card's definition of done and they are authored *before* the card is
dispatched.

You may not edit, skip, weaken, retitle, or delete one. Not to "make it match
the implementation". Not to fix a typo.

If an acceptance test looks wrong, **stop and say so in the PR**. Do not fix
it. `task-lint` fails any diff touching `tests/acceptance/`, and a card that
edits its own definition of done has proven nothing.

Run your acceptance **first**, before writing code. If it is already green,
you are done — change nothing and report `already satisfied`. A card whose
acceptance passes on arrival is a card whose work was carried by a dependency,
and the correct output is the observation.
